      "stageRecord": "Ingen moves from the already established Spec-IP to Spec-CP, leaving a subject trace in Spec-IP. This is A-bar movement into the Swedish declarative prefield; it need not imply a contrastive discourse topic. The resulting subject chain retains its nominative position in Spec-IP and its theta position in Spec-VP. With one constituent in Spec-CP and the finite verb in C, the pronounced order is exactly Ingen såg någonting. The negative quantificational subject c-commands the object, licensing the polarity-sensitive existential use of någonting. Its interpretation is that no person saw anything, not negative concord between two negative DPs. No additional scope movement is required for this reading. The subject's quantificational dependency binds its silent subject positions, and the head-movement chains connect the finite verb to its lower traces; there are no overt anaphors requiring a separate binding analysis.",
